==Reception==
Series 19 received positive reviews from fans and critics. Lottie Townend of ''[[Glasgow University Guardian]]'' said that "the series provided a place of escape and comfort from the difficulties of the outside world. You become personally invested in each contestant’s journey, root for their success and feel the warmth through their shared love for dance".<ref>{{cite news|url=https://glasgowguardian.co.uk/2022/03/18/review-strictly-come-dancing-2021/ |title=Review: Strictly Come Dancing 2021 |website=glasgowguardian.co.uk |date=2022-03-18}}</ref> Jane Rackham of ''[[Radio Times]]'' was positive towards this season's unpredictability, writing: "This must be the most unpredictable series of ''Strictly'' ever. And not only because several participants had to miss a show after testing positive for Covid".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/programme/b-93o97j/strictly-come-dancing-season-19/ |title=Strictly Come Dancing Season 19 |website=radiotimes.com |access-date=2022-10-08}}</ref>

